 ## Background
-DST was introduced in the StyleRF paper [S1]. It is part of a framework for zero-shot 3D style transfer of Neural Radiance Fields. The method builds on the observation that style transformation can be decomposed into sampling-invariant content transformation and deferred style transformation [S1]. It addresses limitations of previous NeRF-based 3D style transfer methods that were computationally intensive or required low-resolution feature maps [S1].
